<title>USA: San Francisco port plans bond-funded developments.</title>
<headline>San Francisco port plans bond-funded developments.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Port of San Francisco plans to build three new parks at a cost of at least $65 million, port officials said on Friday.</p>
<p>The new developments would be financed with revenue bonds supported by port revenues, port spokeswoman Carolyn Macmillan said.</p>
<p>The Port Commission and the Bay Conservation Development Commission were expected to hold public hearings before final approval of the plan, Macmillan said.</p>
